# Monorepo-root build context. Used by every image that builds from HERE:
# dis/services/dis-ui-server/Dockerfile, connectors/thalamus-square/Dockerfile,
# connectors/thalamus-clover/Dockerfile, synapse/Dockerfile and
# synapse/services/synapse-ui-server/Dockerfile.
#
# synapse/Dockerfile joined the list in slice 6b, for the same structural reason the
# connectors are on it: synapse/ is a SIBLING of dis/ in the uv workspace
# ("../synapse"), so a dis/-rooted context cannot reach it.
#
# THIS IS THE ONLY .dockerignore THOSE THREE BUILDS READ. Docker resolves
# .dockerignore at the CONTEXT ROOT (BuildKit also checks a sibling
# `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore`, e.g. `Dockerfile.dockerignore` — NOT a bare
# `.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile). The per-service files at
# connectors/thalamus-{square,clover}/.dockerignore and
# dis/services/dis-ui-server/.dockerignore are therefore INERT for these builds; see
# their headers. Anything that must stay out of those images belongs here.
#
# NOT covered by this file: dis/terraform/docker/{csv-ingest-worker,streaming-consumer}
# .Dockerfile build with a `dis/`-rooted context, and dis/infra/local/fakes.Dockerfile
# builds from `dis/` via docker compose. There is no dis/.dockerignore, so those images
# get no context filtering at all.
#
# --- weight: never a COPY source, ~1.6GB of it -----------------------------------
**/.venv/
**/node_modules/
.git/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.terraform/

# --- dev-only content that WOULD otherwise land in a shipped image ---------------
# The Dockerfiles copy whole package directories (`COPY dis/libs libs`,
# `COPY connectors/sdk /connectors/sdk`), so every one of these rides along unless it
# is excluded here.
#
# Verified against all FIVE root-context builds: none of them needs a tests/ or
# scripts/ directory. Re-verified for synapse in slice 6b — `uv sync --frozen --no-dev
# --package thalamus-synapse` resolves with synapse/tests/ absent, because the wheel
# target is src/synapse and never reaches outside it. Re-verified for the BFF in 8a:
# `uv sync --frozen --no-dev --package synapse-ui-server` resolves with both
# synapse/tests/ and the service's own tests/ absent. uv installs workspace members from `[tool.hatch.build.targets
# .wheel] packages = ["src/<pkg>"]`, which never reaches outside src/.
**/tests/
**/scripts/
**/.env
**/.env.*

# The connectors' dev-only transport and its test doubles. real_transport used to
# import mint_connector_run_id from dev_transport, which dragged dev_transport and
# transitively fakes into the PRODUCTION entrypoint's import graph; the mint now lives
# in its own `run_id` module so these two can be excluded. The Dockerfiles'
# `RUN python -c "import thalamus_<vendor>.real_transport"` is what proves the graph
# stays clean — if either file becomes reachable again, the BUILD fails here rather
# than the container dying on ModuleNotFoundError at start.
#
# Scoped by path rather than `**/dev_transport.py` so this cannot silently reach into
# a future package that legitimately ships a module by either name.
connectors/*/src/*/dev_transport.py
connectors/*/src/*/fakes.py
